---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { campaign } from '../data/campaign';
---
<Layout title="Privacy notice" description="How the No on Measure PFD local website preview handles information.">
  <article class="container prose-page"><h1>Your privacy.</h1><p class="lead">This notice describes the local preview of the No on Measure PFD website.</p><h2>Forms and personal information</h2><p>Signup and contact forms run in your browser for demonstration. Submitting a preview form does not send information to the campaign or a third-party service. The form clears after a valid preview submission. We do not save form data in cookies, browser storage, or a database.</p><p>Please use sample information when reviewing the forms.</p><h2>Analytics and cookies</h2><p>This preview has no analytics, advertising pixels, or tracking cookies. Fonts and images are served locally. The local server may record ordinary request information in its development logs.</p><h2>Email, phone, and external links</h2><p>Email and phone links open your chosen app. If you contact the campaign, your email or phone provider processes that communication. Source links open external websites governed by their own privacy practices. The share button uses your device’s share menu or copies a link to your clipboard.</p><h2>Before a public launch</h2><p>This notice will be updated before live forms or other data collection are enabled. The published notice will identify the information collected, its uses, service providers, retention practices, and how to make privacy requests. Any text messaging program will have separate consent terms.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>Questions about the campaign can be directed to {campaign.contact.name} at <a href={`mailto:${campaign.contact.email}`}>{campaign.contact.email}</a> or <a href={`tel:${campaign.contact.telephone}`}>{campaign.contact.phone}</a>.</p></article>
</Layout>
